[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b2d657-12ba-5244-855a-127cd7306b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(6 e^{2 t} + 6 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536100} {:answer/id #uuid "40d0cfbc-c3e0-5010-8a27-3ad659f00932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(6 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536117} {:answer/id #uuid "a4cbccd4-10a9-5603-9d7c-31e8c4299e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\left(12 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 e^{2 t} - \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536152} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2428f-4efd-534e-b8a5-9d7f8763b84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(12 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536158} {:answer/id #uuid "dcff26e5-35a3-5a9b-8d7d-385dad335180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(6 t e^{2 t} + t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2428f-4efd-534e-b8a5-9d7f8763b84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(12 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536158} :answer-field/id #uuid "07def19c-4051-567c-8664-2166dc149246" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82600b93-632f-5ad5-9122-0f9e18ec5a13" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x^{2} + 3 x y^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + 3 x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + 3 x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x + 3 y^{2})\\,i+6 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=2 e^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+3(2 e^{t})^{2})\\,i+6(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =(12 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+12 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((12 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+12 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((12 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))(\\frac{1}{t})+(12 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{12 e^{2 t}}{t}+24 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =24 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{12 e^{2 t}}{t} + \\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c65a274-bf1c-510e-93f7-af87e6992999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536109} {:answer/id #uuid "2e078f7c-7fb4-5408-83b3-9282edfe1151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(t e^{2 t} + 2 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536114} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd6b5b5-82a5-5bbc-af24-64251de049af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2 t} + 2 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536142} {:answer/id #uuid "a5893d8d-8c9d-58d1-a951-4116dd536f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536154} {:answer/id #uuid "c165d35f-0e3e-54f0-bd59-5e02a049ced0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - e^{2 t} - 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c65a274-bf1c-510e-93f7-af87e6992999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536109} :answer-field/id #uuid "219519b6-e351-5891-9ab3-febd1842d844" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "870cb2f9-447e-5e98-bbd0-de46e4f5add3" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x^{2} + x y^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,i+e^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x + y^{2})\\,i+2 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=e^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+(e^{t})^{2})\\,i+2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =(e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+2 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+e^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+2 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+e^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))(\\frac{1}{t})+(2 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(e^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{e^{2 t}}{t}+2 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =2 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{e^{2 t}}{t} + \\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e4a664-828b-5860-8931-3f7a67e771ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(2 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536113} {:answer/id #uuid "43863874-ca72-58e4-99b6-b2310513b7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4 \\left(4 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 e^{2 t} - \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536119} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9ceac7-621c-54b7-b41f-8994e3294d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\left(2 e^{2 t} + 2 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536123} {:answer/id #uuid "af473d8e-16e9-570c-81d8-5f12c2cd647c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(4 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536155} {:answer/id #uuid "c2579dd5-b29d-546c-85ee-76fc7fc743a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\left(2 t e^{2 t} + t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af473d8e-16e9-570c-81d8-5f12c2cd647c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(4 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536155} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d12e6ff-94be-5dcd-84cc-d93391333c27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e3d3273-ab0d-559d-b480-c40a8896fe51" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 2 x y^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} + 2 x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} + 2 x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(4 x + 2 y^{2})\\,i+4 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=2 e^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(4(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+2(2 e^{t})^{2})\\,i+4(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =(8 e^{2 t} + 4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+8 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((8 e^{2 t} + 4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+8 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((8 e^{2 t} + 4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))(\\frac{1}{t})+(8 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{8 e^{2 t}}{t}+16 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =16 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{8 e^{2 t}}{t} + \\frac{4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51bb9ef3-9793-536d-83c9-dd2d55598726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(e^{4 t} + 2 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536125} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce67cdf-7635-55db-9f92-06eb0b47dfbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(e^{4 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536132} {:answer/id #uuid "6b18450d-20dc-57d6-a4dc-8ccb1ef0781c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(4 t e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{4 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536135} {:answer/id #uuid "94efb8a3-edb0-515f-9afd-69942a6e2b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(t e^{4 t} + t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{2 t}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536150} {:answer/id #uuid "afb69994-495a-5e34-808e-984f82739d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\left(4 t e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - e^{4 t} - \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b18450d-20dc-57d6-a4dc-8ccb1ef0781c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(4 t e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{4 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536135} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b802581-781c-5f13-9c9e-406f2d098414" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6e87588-a6f0-5803-a115-953266b2efe6" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x^{2} + 2 x y^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,i+e^{2 t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + 2 x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + 2 x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x + 2 y^{2})\\,i+4 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=e^{2 t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+2(e^{2 t})^{2})\\,i+4(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(e^{2 t})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 e^{4 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+4 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{2 t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((2 e^{4 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+4 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((2 e^{4 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))(\\frac{1}{t})+(4 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{2 t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{2 e^{4 t}}{t}+8 e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =8 e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{2 e^{4 t}}{t} + \\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125c9fef-e1e6-59ab-a694-d2223cf1b6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536175} {:answer/id #uuid "632784b4-300a-57d6-8fbd-990ee92f3666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2052" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536196} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d9f69-d003-56a1-8175-bb385c5221a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536211} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f82d33-be42-5959-a84f-d0438d80b642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536224} {:answer/id #uuid "e15c611b-dde5-5f8a-b2e4-d0b0be4d5705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d9f69-d003-56a1-8175-bb385c5221a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536211} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac87f4f-c6c9-51ac-93c4-d5e8ee44e66b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "353d7359-1a70-56e3-a4d7-6e5a53fc624b" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=9 y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2},t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,2 \\sqrt{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=9 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(9)(t) \\\\  & =9 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}(9 t)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(8 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}9 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{49}\\frac{9}{8}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(49)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(343)-(1)] \\\\  & =(\\frac{1029}{4})-(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{513}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01df4532-b45d-53b7-a427-d6227daed514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536171} {:answer/id #uuid "859def66-0165-5571-8ffa-7f3709f9ec2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536206} {:answer/id #uuid "a48a6739-81cb-508a-b07a-3a3ab0634724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536214} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cecb10-b5ce-5055-ae8b-93d6718db0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536227} {:answer/id #uuid "dc68bb0d-38dd-5ebb-8d67-8a4394694daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc68bb0d-38dd-5ebb-8d67-8a4394694daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536230} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9c97da8-c43e-5d5d-9311-e6206eff1054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3aeb7177-27b3-5c11-a4d0-3497fd32abae" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=3 y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2},t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3)(t) \\\\  & =3 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(3 t)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(8 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}3 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(9)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(27)-(1)] \\\\  & =(\\frac{27}{4})-(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0494b507-6893-5677-8d04-d371af5154b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536172} {:answer/id #uuid "1987e49f-7e77-5919-82aa-6b139e1177b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{231}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536177} {:answer/id #uuid "2285e068-d56d-5138-acec-6227d8e0efff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{341}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536179} {:answer/id #uuid "2833fcec-8de1-5841-b608-35c960c0bcd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536180} {:answer/id #uuid "eeca22e3-cbf7-5b3d-b018-b1647008ca68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2728}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2285e068-d56d-5138-acec-6227d8e0efff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{341}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536179} :answer-field/id #uuid "852e0dd8-5a52-5753-be99-a707534ca752" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c132797-532b-531b-ac79-d0e890e2f4b0" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=11 y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2},t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{6}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=11 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(11)(t) \\\\  & =11 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}(11 t)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(8 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}11 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{25}\\frac{11}{8}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}[(25)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}[(125)-(1)] \\\\  & =(\\frac{1375}{12})-(\\frac{11}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{341}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57f928b7-f3c1-52b5-b1f3-e51f2ac25685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{14}}{26} + \\frac{45 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536191} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2f52fd-d5a6-5f97-8553-e4f43e399741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 70 \\sqrt{14} + 405 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536192} {:answer/id #uuid "6a2ab4f5-0f77-542a-ae0c-3c24c174ddd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536198} {:answer/id #uuid "de7178fd-a762-590b-a176-d5866a3e8366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536231} {:answer/id #uuid "e54c1709-79ec-5e74-9903-bf87dcc8ae95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de7178fd-a762-590b-a176-d5866a3e8366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536231} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f6f04f0-a3b7-5983-aafe-e6b7a4a0ae76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4598c153-f2b3-5aa3-bf7d-421ba3e4749e" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{3 y + 3 z}{x}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t,t^{2},\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\rangle$ for $t\\in [1,\\sqrt{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2})\\,k$, then along the curve we have $x=t$, $y=t^{2}$, $z=\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(3 t)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^2+(2 t)^2+(3 t)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{3 y + 3 z}{x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{(3)[(t^{2})+(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2})]}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{15}{2})t^2}{(1)t} \\\\  & =\\frac{15 t}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}(\\frac{15 t}{2})(\\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=13 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(26 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{15 t \\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 1}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{14}^{27}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{15}{52}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{52}{\\int }_{14}^{27}u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{52}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{14}^{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{26}[(27)^{3/2}-(14)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{26}[(81 \\sqrt{3})-(14 \\sqrt{14})] \\\\  & =(\\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26})-(\\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13}) \\\\  & =- \\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08930374-f1d2-5c84-b19a-2683f1af6485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 100 \\sqrt{30} + \\frac{1120 \\sqrt{14}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536173} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5c7801-aeea-5abc-8505-a02245d7ee46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{10 \\sqrt{14}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536201} {:answer/id #uuid "af8bd43c-2eb0-5278-8be1-06e077eda466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{50 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{560 \\sqrt{14}}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536217} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e839ff-7be3-5f5c-93ae-9e4bc0b08ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/valu